    "title": "Chequamegon Challenge bike races slated Aug. 2 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The Chequamegon Area Mountain Bike Association (CAMBA) will host one of the Midwest’s most iconic mountain bike endurance races, the Chequamegon Challenge, Saturday Aug. 2 along the singletrack of the Sawyer and Bayfield County Forests and the Chequamegon-Nicolet National Forest. The event celebrates the CAMBA Trail System. Participants can choose between 30K, 50K and 100K races. Registration is online through 7 p.m. Friday Aug. 1. There is no Saturday morning registration. Bib pickup will be from 4-7 p.m. Friday at New Moon Bike & Ski in Hayward and at the S.C. Johnson Outdoor Center at the Hwy. 00 trailhead from 6-8:30 a.m. Saturday. All races will start at 9 a.m. Saturday behind the S.C. Johnson Outdoor Center. Subscribe to the Sawyer County Record",
